_id": "chatcmpl-7d77888c-f7d7-4f3b-894c-45ac15e29f88", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {\"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"## 1) Inspection \\u2014 what is actually here\\n\\nPresent:\\n- `/workspace` contains exactly one file, `task.json` (412 B). It holds the question, the context string, and `documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"` **There is no `track.md` file on disk** \\u2014 that document exists only as a string inside `task.json`.\\n- Python 3.14.4 at `python3`; pip 25.1.1 present at `/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pip`.\\n\\nPlainly absent (verified, not assumed):\\n- **No CycleNet code anywhere** (`find / -iname \\\"*cyclenet*\\\"` \\u2192 nothing). No model source, no config, no scripts.\\n- **No time-series data**: `datasets: []` in the brief; no `/data`, `/opt`, `/srv`; the only `*.csv` on the filesystem are OS/vendor files (ieee OUI, distro info). No ETT/Weather/Traffic/Electricity/Pems files.\\n- **No scientific stack**: `numpy`, `scipy`, `pandas`, `statsmodels`, `sklearn`, `torch`, `matplotlib` all raise `ModuleNotFoundError`. Only `setuptools`/`pip` wheels exist under `/usr/share/python-wheels`.\\n- **No network**: DNS resolution fails (`Temporary failure in name resolution`), so pip cannot install anything; no local pip cache or wheels to bootstrap from.\\n- **No GPU** (per brief); `cpu_affinity_count: 224`.\\n\\nConsequence for the design (flag now, details later): the experiment as designed must (a) treat data acquisition and dependency installation as explicit, currently-failing prerequisites, and (b) carry a **fully offline fallback** \\u2014 synthetic series with known ground-truth period (generatable with stdlib `math`/`random`, since even `numpy` is missing) plus a hand-coded ACF \\u2014 so the core ACF\\u2192L identification logic is testable with zero external dependencies. This is what makes the design executable in this sandbox rather t