{"id": "78fada16-dc80-453f-af53-d8c97b0253c8", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:46:44.000232", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "10c8b4a8-fc21-489b-9ea5-6f1cda751c8f", "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-909bb5ec2dfb772b", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"phase\": \"exploration\", \"command\": \"cd /workspace/probe && python3 - <<'PY'\\ns=open('acf_logic_check.py').read()\\ns=s.replace(\\\"if r[k]>=r[k-1] and r[k]>r[k+1] and r[k]>ci:\\\",\\\"if r[k-1]>=r[k-2] and r[k-1]>r[k] and r[k-1]>ci:\\\")\\ns=s.replace(\\\"            if abs(j/m-k)<=max(1,round(0.02*k)): alias=True\\\",\\\"            if abs(j/m-k)<=max(1,round(0.02*k)): alias=True\\\")\\ns=s.replace('r=acf(noise(N,1.0),500)','r=acf(noise(N,1.0),500)')\\ns=s.replace('print(\\\"T3 strong trend, RAW: naive argmax lag=\\\",r.index(max(r))+1,\\\"(true=24)\\\")','print(\\\"T3 strong trend, RAW: naive argmax lag=\\\",r.index(max(r))+1,\\\"(true=24)\\\")')\\nopen('acf2.py','w').write(s)\\nPY\\ntimeout 600 python3 acf2.py\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 32.458, \"output\": \"T1 pure sinusoid P=24: top5 peaks [(984, 1.0), (960, 1.0), (936, 1.0), (912, 1.0), (888, 1.0)] after dedup [984, 960, 936] acf_time_s=0.28\\nT2 white noise: max|r|=0.0374  CI=+-0.0219  exceedances=31\\nT3 strong trend, RAW: naive argmax lag= 1 (true=24)\\n   detrended(MA49): top peaks [312, 336, 168] -> primary 312\\nT4 dual 24+168: top peaks [(336, 0.997), (504, 0.997), (168, 0.997), (359, 0.751), (527, 0.751)] after dedup [336, 504, 359]\\nT5 dual 24+50 (coprime): top peaks [(551, 0.982), (49, 0.982), (97, 0.939), (503, 0.939), (146, 0.872)] after dedup [551, 49, 97]\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "10c8b4a8-fc21-489b-9ea5-6f1cda751c8f", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
{"id": "de77b62d-b039-4d98-9c3d-a7882a184ef5", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:47:38.648858", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "78fada16-dc80-453f-af53-d8c97b0253c8", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Two genuinely important methodological findings from the probe (naive argmax-ACF is degenerate for near-sinusoidal series; harmonic de-dup as commonly coded keeps the wrong end of the ladder). Let me pin down the rule that fixes them, then write the design."}], "reasoning_content": "Interesting and useful: T3/T4/T5 show a genuine phenomenon — high-lag beats (multiples) dominate because ACF at large lags near multiples is high, and among multiples of 24 the tie is broken by tiny numerical/noise fluctuations, so \"argmax ACF\" picks an arbitrary high multiple (312 = 13*24, 336=14*24, 551 ≈ 11*50=550... 551 hmm). Also T5: 49 ≈ 50. This shows the \"fundamental vs harmonic\" degeneracy: for a nearly-sinusoidal series, ALL multiples of the true period have near-identical ACF. So argmax-ACF without a max-lag cap / with high L_max is degenerate → must define candidate extraction as *smallest* significant peak above threshold (first strong peak), or restrict L_max. And the harmonic de-dup as I coded it (suppress k if k ≈ j/m) actually keeps the LARGEST multiple and suppresses the fundamental! That's backwards for choosing L. Important design insight: de-dup must be \"keep the smallest lag that explains larger peaks as its multiples\" (i.e., fundamental selection), not \"keep largest\".\n\nT2 white noise: 31 exceedances out of 500 lags vs expected ~25 at 5% — roughly consistent, and it shows the naive ±1.96/√N CI under-counts for autocorrelated series (I used pure noise; 31/500 slightly over, expected 25, sd≈4.9, so within ~1.2 sd — fine). Also key point: the naive CI gives false peaks — motivates Bartlett/robust CI.\n\nGreat, these are genuine methodological findings for the design's controls, and I discovered them legitimately. Let me run one more small probe to confirm the \"smallest significant peak\" rule and cap-L_max fix, plus a check that naive argmax under strong trend picks lag 1 (yes T3 showed lag=1 for raw with trend — wait it says naive argmax lag = 1 for the raw trended series, hmm k index: r.index(max(r))+1 = 1 means lag 1 ACF ≈ max → trend dominance confirmed: raw ACF is monotone-ish, argmax at lag 1, so raw ACF totally fails with trend. Good — that's evidence that preprocessing matters, exactly the arm (ii) the researcher wants.)\n\nLet me do a quick third probe: fundamental-selection rule (smallest lag with ACF ≥ 0.5*max among lags ≥ some min, or smallest lag whose ACF exceeds CI and is ≥ 90% of max ACF within L_max cap) on the dual cases, and test sensitivity to L_max. Also test seasonal differencing sensitivity. Keep it short — maybe 1 probe run.\n\nActually, careful about scope: researcher wants a design, not a run. But these small logic probes serve as feasibility evidence and, more valuably, as pre-registration of extractor rules (I now know the naive rules are degenerate). One more probe to nail the recommended rule, then write the design. Let me make it fast (kmax 400, N 4000).\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cd /workspace/probe && cat > acf3.py <<'PY'\nimport math,random,time\nrnd=random.Random(11)\ndef ar1(n,s,phi=0.6):\n    o=[];e=0.0\n    for _ in range(n): e=phi*e+rnd.gauss(0,s); o.append(e)\n    return o\ndef acf(x,kmax):\n    n=len(x);m=sum(x)/n;d=[v-m for v in x];c0=sum(v*v for v in d)/n\n    return [(sum(d[i]*d[i+k] for i in range(n-k))/(n-k))/c0 for k in range(1,kmax+1)]\ndef ma(x,w):\n    h=w//2;n=len(x);cs=[0.0]*(n+1)\n    for i,v in enumerate(x): cs[i+1]=cs[i]+v\n    return [x[i]-(cs[min(n,i+h+1)]-cs[max(0,i-h)])/(min(n,i+h+1)-max(0,i-h)) for i in range(n)]\n\n# FUNDAMENTAL rule: smallest lag k>=kmin with r[k] >= frac * max(r[1..Lmax]), r[k] > CI\ndef fundamental(r,kmin=2,frac=0.90,ci=0.0):\n    if not r: return None\n    mx=max(r[:max(1,int(os)]) if False else r)\n    for k in range(kmin,len(r)+1):\n        if r[k-1]>=frac*mx and r[k-1]>ci: return k\n    return None\n\ndef report(name,x,true_p,P):\n    r=acf(x,P)\n    naive=r.index(max(r))+1\n    f=fundamental(r,2,0.90)\n    f50=fundamental(r,2,0.50)\n    print(\"%-28s Lmax=%4d  naive_argmax=%4d  fundamental@0.90=%s  fundamental@0.50=%s  true=%s\"%(name,P,naive,f,f50,true_p))\n\nN=6000\nfor p in (24,50,96,168):\n    x=[math.sin(2*math.pi*i/p)+ar1(N,0.02)[i] for i in range(N)]\n    report(\"single P=%d (no trend)\"%p, x, p, 400)\nxt=[math.sin(2*math.pi*i/24)+0.02*i+ar1(N,0.02)[i] for i in range(N)]\nreport(\"P=24 RAW +trend\", xt, 24, 400)\nreport(\"P=24 detrended(MA49)\", ma(xt,49), 24, 400)\nz=[math.sin(2*math.pi*i/24)+1.5*math.sin(2*math.pi*i/168)+ar1(N,0.05)[i] for i in range(N)]\nzd=ma(z,337)\nfor P in (200,400,800,1200):\n    r=acf(zd,P); print(\"dual 24+168 detrended  Lmax=%4d  naive=%4d  fund@0.90=%s fund@0.50=%s (expect 168 primary, 24 secondary)\"%(P,r.index(max(r))+1,fundamental(r,2,0.9),fundamental(r,2,0.5)))\nprint(\"T2 repeat: white-noise false-positive rate at naive +-%.3f CI, 20 series x 300 lags:\"%(1.96/math.sqrt(N)))\ntot=0\nfor s in range(20):\n    rr=random.Random(100+s); rnd=rr\n    x=[rr.gauss(0,1) for _ in range(N)]\n    tot+=sum(1 for v in acf(x,300) if abs(v)>1.96/math.sqrt(N))\nprint(\"   mean exceedances per series = %.1f of 300 (nominal 5%% = 15.0)\"%(tot/20))\nPY\ntimeout 900 python3 acf3.py", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8572587e9395c266", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-8572587e9395c266", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/probe && cat > acf3.py <<'PY'\\nimport math,random,time\\nrnd=random.Random(11)\\ndef ar1(n,s,phi=0.6):\\n    o=[];e=0.0\\n    for _ in range(n): e=phi*e+rnd.gauss(0,s); o.append(e)\\n    return o\\ndef acf(x,kmax):\\n    n=len(x);m=sum(x)/n;d