{"id": "80bd7635-f240-4142-95f8-0fbd6acb1a46", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:49:25.223759", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "1803f748-fc9b-49fb-a984-90b4650e2b09", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Very informative. Key findings (all on synthetic data, in-sandbox, zero deps):\n\n1. Naive argmax-ACF is degenerate for near-sinusoidal series: P=24 → argmax 168 (=7×24); P=50 → 100 (=2×50); P=24 with trend → lag 1; dual 24+168 with Lmax=800 → 672 (=4×168). So naive argmax returns an arbitrary high harmonic. Confirmed.\n\n2. My \"fundamental@0.90\" rule (smallest lag with r ≥ 0.9·max) fails badly because with AR(1) noise, r at lag 2 is already ~0.98 of max (AR persistence inflates short-lag ACF). So the \"smallest lag above fraction of max\" rule is broken by short-lag persistence — needs either (a) prominence/local-max requirement (must be a local maximum, not just above a level), and (b) exclusion/whitening of the short-lag AR component (that's exactly why PACF and seasonal differencing are needed). So the extractor must be: local maxima only + significance (Bartlett CI) + prominence relative to intervening troughs + then pick smallest lag among near-maximal peaks (within ε of global max, or the smallest lag k such that all larger near-maximal peaks are integer multiples of k).\n\n3. Also note detrended P=24 case: fundamental@0.90 gave 23 (off-by-one? no: local max check absent, 23 is on the plateau of the sinusoid ACF near-max at lag 23 = 0.966... wait the ACF of sinusoid at 23 ≈ cos(2π·23/24)=0.966 ≥ 0.9·1.0 → picked 23. Yes: monotone rising region. Confirms the need for a strict local-max requirement.)\n\n4. White noise false positive rate: 16.6/300 ≈ 5.5% vs nominal 5% — the naive ±1.96/√N CI is roughly calibrated for white noise (slightly liberal) but is known to be far too liberal for autocorrelated series; the design should therefore use Bartlett-adjusted or effective-sample-size CIs. Good empirical anchor.\n\nLet me run one final refined extractor to demonstrate a rule that works: local-max + prominence + integer-multiple-consistency + short-lag guard. Quick, cheap, and it lets me state the pre-registered extractor algorithm as \"logic-check passed\" rather than untested. Let me do it once, cleanly.\n\nRule draft:\n- compute ACF to Lmax (cap: min(N/4, 4*H_max, 1000)).\n- mask lag region: kmin = 2.\n- local maxima: r[k] > r[k±1] with a tolerance window w=2 (r[k] = max in window ±2), and r[k] > CI_bartlett(k).\n- prominence: r[k] - min(r between k and nearest higher peak) ≥ prom_abs (0.1) or relative.\n- near-max set: peaks with r[k] ≥ (1-ε)·max_peak_r, ε=0.05.\n- fundamental selection: among near-max peaks, choose the smallest k such that ≥70% of near-max peaks are within ±2% of integer multiples of k. Otherwise fall back to smallest near-max peak.\n- secondary: the largest near-max peak that is not within ±2% of a multiple of primary and exceeds CI.\n- Short-lag guard: require k ≥ kmin where kmin = first lag after which ACF drops below CI (i.e., skip the AR persistence region: kmin = 1 + last consecutive lag with r > CI before a dip). Actually simpler: require that the candidate is a local max, which naturally excludes monotone persistence decay. Let's test.\n\nLet me implement and test on all the synthetic cases including seasonal + AR + trend, plus a case where the true period has strong harmonic content.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cd /workspace/probe && cat > acf4.py <<'PY'\nimport math,random\ndef acf(x,kmax):\n    n=len(x);m=sum(x)/n;d=[v-m for v in x];c0=sum(v*v for v in d)/n\n    return [(sum(d[i]*d[i+k] for i in range(n-k))/(n-k))/c0 for k in range(1,kmax+1)]\ndef ma(x,w):\n    h=w//2;n=len(x);cs=[0.0]*(n+1)\n    for i,v in enumerate(x): cs[i+1]=cs[i]+v\n    return [x[i]-(cs[min(n,i+h+1)]-cs[max(0,i-h)])/(min(n,i+h+1)-max(0,i-h)) for i in range(n)]\ndef bartlett_r_ci(r,k,z=1.96):  # Bartlett-adjusted band for a stationary series\n    s=1.0+2.0*sum(v*v for v in r[:k]) if k>0 else 1.0\n    return z*math.sqrt(s/len(r))\ndef extract(x,Lmax,prom=0.10,eps=0.05,w=2,mult_tol=0.02,cov=0.7):\n    r=acf(x,Lmax); n=len(x); ci0=1.96/math.sqrt(n)\n    pk=[]\n    for k in range(max(2,w+1),Lmax-w):\n        win=[r[j-1] for j in range(k-w,k+w+1)]\n        if r[k-1]==max(win) and r[k-1]>ci0 and r[k-1]>0:\n            pk.append((k,r[k-1]))\n    if not pk: return None,None,ci0,0\n    mx=max(v for _,v in pk)\n    near=[(k,v) for k,v in pk if v>=(1-eps)*mx]\n    def fund(cands):\n        best=None\n        for k,_ in sorted(cands):\n            hit=sum(1 for j,_ in cands if any(abs(j-k*m)<=max(2,mult_tol*k*m) for m in range(1,15)))\n            if hit/len(cands)>=cov: return k\n        return sorted(cands)[0][0]\n    prim=fund(near)\n    sec=[(k,v) for k,v in sorted(near) if k!=prim and not any(abs(k-prim*m)<=max(2,mult_tol*prim*m) for m in range(2,15))]\n    return prim,(sec[0][0] if sec else None),ci0,len(pk)\n\ndef gen(seed,p,amp=1.0,p2=None,amp2=0.0,trend=0.0,ar=0.7,noise=0.15,N=8000,harm=0.4):\n    rr=random.Random(seed); e=0.0; o=[]\n    for i in range(N):\n        e=ar*e+rr.gauss(0,noise)\n        v=amp*(math.sin(2*math.pi*i/p)+harm*math.sin(4*math.pi*i/p))+e+trend*i\n        if p2: v+=amp2*math.sin(2*math.pi*i/p2)\n        o.append(v)\n    return o\n\ncases=[(\"single P=24\",dict(p=24),24,None),(\"single P=50\",dict(p=50),50,None),\n       (\"single P=96\",dict(p=96),96,None),(\"single P=168\",dict(p=168),168,None),\n       (\"P=24 +trend\",dict(p=24,trend=0.02),24,None),\n       (\"P=24 low SNR\",dict(p=24,noise=0.9,ar=0.7),24,None),\n       (\"dual 24+168 (w24 amp1)\",dict(p=24,p2=168,amp2=1.5),168,24),\n       (\"dual 50+168\",dict(p=50,p2=168,amp2=1.5),168,50)]\nfor name,kw,tp,ts in cases:\n    for det in (0,1):\n        x=gen(3,**kw); y=ma(x,2*tp+1) if det else x\n        Lmax=1000\n        prim,sec,ci,npk=extract(y,Lmax)\n        tag=\"detrended\" if det else \"raw     \"\n        exact = \"OK \" if prim==tp else (\"near\" if 